Vendored so the viewer works offline. Fetched from jsDelivr, unmodified.

three.min.js       three.js r128 (three@0.128.0/build/three.min.js)         MIT   LICENSE-three.txt
OrbitControls.js   three.js r128 (examples/js/controls/OrbitControls.js)     MIT   same licence
d3.min.js          d3 7.9.0 (d3@7.9.0/dist/d3.min.js)                        ISC   LICENSE-d3.txt

r128 is the last three.js line with a classic-script build and a global OrbitControls, which keeps the app free of
a bundler and of import maps (Chrome and Safari both load it). d3 is ISC-licensed (permissive, MIT-equivalent
terms), not MIT or BSD as often assumed; the licence text is kept alongside.

GLTFLoader.js     three.js r128 (examples/js/loaders/GLTFLoader.js)         MIT   same licence
models/kid.glb    Microsoft Rocketbox avatar Male_Child_02 (github.com/microsoft/Microsoft-Rocketbox)   MIT   LICENSE-rocketbox.txt
                  Modified by squashvid/viewer/figure_model.py: bones renamed to Mixamo names, a head-top bone added,
                  textures resized to 1024 px, exported as glTF. view3d.js loads it with GLTFLoader on demand.
models/kid_mask_body.png, kid_mask_head.png  made by figure_model.py from the avatar's textures: which pixels are
                  shirt, shorts and skin.
